course: dictionary
lesson: 15839
title: Feeling silly: the word undignified
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Dignified means calm, proper and serious. Undignified means the opposite: the un- at the start means not, so undignified means not dignified. «Sam slipped in the puddle and sat down in the mud.» Sam looks silly and embarrassed, so that moment was undignified.
explain: Look at the words around the word to find its meaning. Ask yourself: what would fit here? In «Toad hated being thrown into the canal, because it was so undignified», the word undignified tells you how Toad felt about being thrown in. Try your meaning in the sentence: silly and embarrassing makes sense.
explain: Undignified often describes a moment, not a person. A person can have an undignified moment, even if they are usually calm and proper. That is why undignified is a feelings word in stories.
fact: Undignified means making you look silly or embarrassed.
fact: Undignified also means not calm, proper or serious.
fact: The un- at the start means not, so undignified is the opposite of dignified.
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, Toad hates undignified moments, like being thrown into the canal by the barge-woman.
fact: Alice feels undignified when she grows and shrinks.
exercise: «Sam slipped in the puddle and came up covered in mud.» What does undignified mean? | Sad and tired | Calm and very proper | Quick and clever | *Making you look silly and embarrassed
exercise: Toad hated being thrown into the canal because it was so ____. Which word fills the gap? | quiet | happy | calm | *undignified
exercise: What does the un- at the start of undignified mean? | very | again | *not | before
test: «Alice felt undignified when she grew so tall that her head hit the ceiling.» What does undignified mean here? | Proud and calm | Very quiet | *Making her look silly and awkward | Hungry
test: Which word means the opposite of undignified? | Muddy | Silly | Embarrassed | *Dignified
exam: «The mayor slipped on a banana skin during his speech and landed in a puddle.» Why is this fall undignified? | *Because it made him look silly in front of everyone | Because he stayed calm and in control | Because it made him rich | Because it was very quiet
